    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nHi! Thanks for your awesome project! \r\n\r\nFound a small bug for `mini.starter` with `current_dir` option turned on. Problem: files from other dirs, that have a name of current dir as a prefix, are shown in `starter` window.\r\n\r\nIf you think that this should be fixed, I can make a PR. \n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n0. `mini.starter` plugin is enabled, with item `starter.sections.recent_files(5, true, true),`\r\n1. `mkdir foo`\r\n2. `mkdir foobar`\r\n3. `nvim foobar/a.txt`\r\n4. Quit nvim with `:x`\r\n5. `cd foo`\r\n6. `nvim` \r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEmpty list of recent files.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`a.txt` is shown,  while belonging to other directory",
