            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski thank you for quick fixes! It's fine by me, but I think Windows users may have issues, as paths there use `\\\\` separator, not `/`.\r\n\r\nIf I remember correctly, Neovim and Vim use `/` as separator for file paths on any platform. This basically boils down to how file paths are stored in `v:oldfiles`. As I can not test on Windows, we'll have to wait and see if anyone complaining.",
